{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "meta": {
    "title": "diagrammer",
    "subtitle": "This repository as a hierarchy of its four stages: a top level that is a map rather than a census"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "origin": "modelReviewed",
    "note": "A worked example of what stage 2 produces when it is done well, and the only model here that is one. It describes this repository, read from its own stage-1 graph: every package, file count and import relation in it was taken from that graph rather than remembered. What it demonstrates is the part `diagrammer instruct` asks a model to judge and no schema can state. Seven components at the top rather than the sixteen packages the graph holds, grouped by the stage of the pipeline each belongs to, so that the first page is a map of the program and the detail is a click away. diagrammer.codegraph.json beside it is an earlier, shallower model of the same repository. Both are kept, because the difference between them is the lesson: this one states twenty-six relationships across five pages where that one states fourteen across three, and both draw everything they state."
  },
